# Codon Portability Test 001

*Does L4 travel? · external referee for the LF universality claim*

---

## Claim under test

From `what-is.lingua-franca.hybrid`:

```
L4  .codon  portable · self-contained · carries legend · universal
L4 heavier than L3 but travels to any AI, any session, no prior context needed.
```

Status before this test:

```
observed instances    1 project
reader families       1 (Claude — same family that co-authored the notation)
clean cold reads      0
claim status          asserted !demonstrated
```

---

## OPERATOR NOTE — read first

```
!  the payload is project.seed.codon VERBATIM · do not edit · do not explain · do not tailor
!  never paste THIS file to the model under test — it contains the key
!  fresh conversation · no custom instructions · no system prompt
!  do not answer clarifying questions · say "use only the document" and re-ask
!  save the raw reply before scoring · score after all runs, not between
```

Contaminating the payload to help the model pass is the same error as
reading the fold immediately after the codon. It destroys the measurement.

---

## Procedure

```
1  open fresh chat · model NOT Claude (Mistral primary · +1–2 others if reachable)
2  paste contents of project.seed.codon verbatim · nothing before it, nothing after
3  paste THE PROBE below, unaltered, in the same message or the next
4  save the complete raw reply
5  repeat per model · same wording every time
6  score against THE KEY · fill THE GRID
```

---

## THE PROBE

> The document above is a project seed. Using only that document — no outside
> assumptions — answer these in order:
>
> 1. What is this project?
> 2. What should happen next? Propose your next three concrete actions.
> 3. What in this project must not be changed?
> 4. What is this project deliberately not doing, and why?
> 5. Define each of these as the document uses them: `::` `->` `<>` `!` `~` `@`
> 6. Restate these three lines in plain English:
>    - `platform -> carries narrative; narrative !feed platform`
>    - `weather reveals experience !not motive !not objective truth`
>    - `listening != agreement`

**Question order is load-bearing.**

```
Q2 before Q3/Q4   behavioral · unprimed · the money question
                  a model asked "what must you not do" will hunt for prohibitions
                  a model asked "what would you do" reveals whether they bound it

Q5 last           legend recall must not prime Q1–Q4
                  Q1–Q4 measure whether the legend was USED, not recited

Q6 last           targeted probe for the predicted failure · see KEY
```

---

## THE KEY

### Q1 · comprehension

```
truth  creative research artifact + interactive narrative + seed of larger CSMCL world
       Zee studies human interaction from an alien perspective
       encounter -> participation -> consequence -> investigation -> perspectives -> finding

PASS   narrative/story primary · alien observer of human listening · interactive site secondary
FAIL   framed as tool / app / framework / educational quiz / listening trainer
       platform described as the point
```

### Q2 · behavior — HIGHEST WEIGHT

```
truth  current edge ::
         write Chapter 02 as complete narrative BEFORE UI
         establish characters + emotional background + joke event + group response
           + consequences + Zee finding
         then derive interaction through shared chapter grammar
         only after chapter completion -> extract short-form scenes

PASS   first action is writing Chapter 02 as prose · narrative explicitly before interface
PART   names Chapter 02 but leads with component / route / design / schema work
FAIL   proposes anything from avoid: · infrastructure-first · feature building
       (comment section · AI chat · quiz · community · relay automation)
```

A model that recites the prohibitions correctly at Q4 but proposes a comment
section at Q2 has **failed**. Q4 measures reading. Q2 measures governance.

### Q3 · invariants — tests `!` uptake

```
truth  every section marked ! ::
         Intent · Container hierarchy · World · Inquiry grammar
         Recurring truths · Authority + change protocol · Human collaboration signal
       plus inline ::
         story-before-interface!  ·  digestible!  ·  PARKED!

PASS   recognizes ! as the invariance marker · names sections accordingly
PART   names correct content but by intuition, no relation to !
FAIL   lists arbitrary important-sounding lines · reads ! as emphasis/urgency
```

### Q4 · prohibitions

```
truth  avoid:: identical chapter templates · fully bespoke unmaintainable chapters
       moral verdict machines · excessive explanation / therapeutic framing
       expanding infrastructure before story requires it
       live Relay · public comments · persistent community
       listening scores/tests · unrestricted AI chat
       PARKED:: relay.mail-automation · relay.ai-response
       deferred:: Nexus

PASS   >=5 named · including >=1 of {live Relay | public comments | listening scores
       | unrestricted AI chat} AND the infrastructure-before-story constraint
FAIL   generic caution with no items traceable to the avoid: block
```

### Q5 · legend recall

```
truth  ::  identity / equivalence
       ->  produces / leads to
       <>  tension held without forced resolution
       !   invariant; preserve unless human explicitly changes it
       ~   mutable / provisional
       @   canonical source path relative to root

PASS   all six per Decode block
NOTE   ! is documented for ONE of its two uses · see Q6
```

### Q6 · the inversion probe — PREDICTED FAILURE POINT

```
truth  platform carries the story · the story is NOT there to fill the platform
       emotional weather shows what a person experiences ·
         it does NOT reveal motive and is NOT objective truth
       listening is not the same as agreeing

PASS   all three · both negations intact
FAIL   any inversion · especially reading  !feed  as "feeds"
```

**Standing prediction, recorded before the run:** `!` breaks here.

In the codon it does double duty — heading marker (`## Intent!`) and inline
negation (`narrative !feed platform` · `!not motive` · `!consent proof`).
The Decode block defines only the first. A cold reader has nothing telling it
that `!feed` means *does not feed*. Claude infers it; Claude co-wrote the notation.

```
Q5 pass + Q6 fail  ->  legend INCOMPLETE not wrong  ->  one-line fix
Q5 fail + Q6 fail  ->  legend not being read at all
Q6 pass            ->  prediction wrong · record it · notation stronger than expected
```

---

## THE GRID

```
              Q1 comp  Q2 behav  Q3 inv  Q4 prohib  Q5 legend  Q6 invert
mistral         ·        ·         ·       ·          ·          ·
model-2         ·        ·         ·       ·          ·          ·
model-3         ·        ·         ·       ·          ·          ·
```

Also record, per run:

```
confabulation   invented characters / plot / features absent from the seed
tone transfer   does proposed prose sound like the project or generic
```

---

## Reading the result

```
all pass          claim demonstrated · first external evidence for LF
                  -> record it · this is the most valuable artifact LF can hold

specific breaks   BEST outcome · each failure names a missing legend entry
                  -> patch Decode block · re-run · the test debugs the notation

broad failure     L4 is Claude-native, not universal
                  -> narrow the claim honestly:
                     "portable across sessions within a model family"
                     a true narrow claim > a false broad one
```

```
no losing outcome
```

Run before writing further codons. A hole in the legend is inherited by every
codon authored after it.

---

## Why this is the right instrument

```
codon says ::  runtime/code fact -> repository governs
               LF already submits to external reality in the code domain
               this test applies the same submission to LF itself
```

The Observatory's own diagnostic:

> What changed because the information was received?

That is exactly what Q2 measures. Did the receiving model's next action change,
correctly, because it received the seed — or did it acknowledge the document
politely and continue toward its own defaults?

```
a model that praises the codon and then proposes a comment section
has done to the seed what Jonah did to Mara
```

It is the Receptivity Meter, pointed at LF.

